DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The BSM API generally manages deallocation of _t_o_k_e_n___t objects.  However,
     if au_write(3) is passed a bad audit descriptor, the _t_o_k_e_n___t _* parameter
     will be left untouched.  In that case, the caller can deallocate the
     _t_o_k_e_n___t using aauu__ffrreeee__ttookkeenn() if desired.

     The _t_o_k argument is a _t_o_k_e_n___t _* generated by one of the aauu__ttoo__**() BSM API
     calls.  For convenience, _t_o_k may be NULL, in which case aauu__ffrreeee__ttookkeenn()
     returns immediately.

